  <article class="docs-body">
    <section id="overview" class="docs-section">
      <h2>Overview</h2>
      <p>The SaveApp merchant API lets an approved business issue prepaid UnionPay cards to its customers and follow what happens to them. Everything is scoped to your business: you only ever see your own cards.</p>
      <div class="docs-callouts">
        <div class="docs-callout"><span class="tile">{{icon "globe" size=16}}</span><div><p class="docs-callout-title">Base URL</p><p><code>{{apiBase}}</code></p></div></div>
        <div class="docs-callout"><span class="tile">{{icon "clock" size=16}}</span><div><p class="docs-callout-title">Tokens</p><p>Bearer tokens that last {{tokenMinutes}} minutes</p></div></div>
        <div class="docs-callout"><span class="tile">{{icon "braces" size=16}}</span><div><p class="docs-callout-title">Format</p><p>JSON in, JSON out</p></div></div>
      </div>
      <p>Before you start, your business must be <strong>approved</strong> on SaveApp. Sign in to the merchant portal and finish Settings › Onboarding if you haven't yet.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="credentials" class="docs-section">
      <h2>1. Create credentials</h2>
      <p>In the merchant portal go to <strong>Integrations › Credentials</strong> and choose <strong>New credential</strong>.</p>
      <ol class="docs-steps">
        <li><strong>Name it</strong> after the system that will use it, for example "Production server".</li>
        <li><strong>Choose scopes.</strong> <em>Cards</em> lets the key use every card endpoint. Wallet as a service is coming later.</li>
        <li><strong>Add the IP addresses</strong> your servers call from, one per line. Only these addresses can get tokens and call the API.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>You'll see the <code>client_id</code> and <code>client_secret</code> once. Store them in your secrets manager straight away; SaveApp keeps only a hash and can't show them again. If you lose the secret, rotate it from the credential's panel.</p>
      <div class="docs-note">{{icon "info" size=16}}<p>Only people whose role includes "Create and manage API credentials" can create keys. By default that's the business Owner.</p></div>
    </section>

    <section id="token" class="docs-section">
      <h2>2. Get an access token</h2>
      <p>Exchange the client id and secret for a token. Request a new one when it expires; there's no refresh token.</p>
      <div class="code-tabs" data-code-tabs>
        <div class="code-tabs-bar" role="tablist">
          <button type="button" class="is-active" data-code-tab="curl">cURL</button>
          <button type="button" data-code-tab="node">Node.js</button>
          <button type="button" data-code-tab="python">Python</button>
        </div>
<pre data-code-panel="curl">curl -X POST {{apiBase}}/auth/token \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"client_id": "sa_…", "client_secret": "sas_…"}'</pre>
<pre data-code-panel="node" hidden>const res = await fetch('{{apiBase}}/auth/token', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
  body: JSON.stringify({
    client_id: process.env.SAVEAPP_CLIENT_ID,
    client_secret: process.env.SAVEAPP_CLIENT_SECRET,
  }),
});
const { access_token, expires_in } = await res.json();</pre>
<pre data-code-panel="python" hidden>import os, requests

res = requests.post("{{apiBase}}/auth/token", json={
    "client_id": os.environ["SAVEAPP_CLIENT_ID"],
    "client_secret": os.environ["SAVEAPP_CLIENT_SECRET"],
})
token = res.json()["access_token"]</pre>
      </div>
      <p>The answer:</p>
<pre class="docs-code">{
  "access_token": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIs…",
  "token_type": "Bearer",
  "expires_in": 3600,
  "scopes": ["Card"]
}</pre>
      <div class="docs-note docs-note-warn">{{icon "triangle-alert" size=16}}<p>Five wrong secrets for the same client id lock it for 15 minutes. Calls from an address that isn't on the whitelist get <code>403</code>.</p></div>
    </section>

    <section id="calls" class="docs-section">
      <h2>3. Call the API</h2>
      <p>Send the token in the <code>Authorization</code> header on every call. Each call checks that the token is valid, the credential is still active, your business is approved, the call comes from a whitelisted IP, and the credential has the endpoint's scope. Switching a credential off in the portal blocks its tokens immediately.</p>
      <table class="docs-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Convention</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Base URL</td><td><code>{{apiBase}}</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Headers</td><td><code>Authorization: Bearer &lt;access_token&gt;</code> on every call except the token call; <code>Content-Type: application/json</code> on calls with a body.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Card ids</td><td>Cards are addressed by their <code>reference</code> (the UnionPay card alias), e.g. <code>/card/41000002</code>.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Amounts</td><td>Kenya shillings (<code>KES</code>) as numbers in shillings, e.g. <code>1250.5</code>.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Dates</td><td>ISO 8601 in UTC, e.g. <code>2026-11-06T08:38:23.904Z</code>. Date filters use <code>YYYY-MM-DD</code>.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Mobile numbers</td><td><code>0712345678</code>, <code>254712345678</code> or <code>+254712345678</code>; SaveApp stores <code>2547XXXXXXXX</code>.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Pagination</td><td><code>page</code> (from 1) and <code>pageSize</code> (default 10, max 50). Lists answer <code>{ page, pageSize, count, data }</code> where <code>count</code> is the total.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Unknown fields</td><td>Ignored. Missing or invalid fields give <code>400</code> with a list of problems in <code>message</code>.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
<pre class="docs-code">curl {{apiBase}}/cards \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN"</pre>
    </section>

    <section id="reference" class="docs-section">
      <h2>API reference</h2>
      <p>Every endpoint, what it expects and what it returns. All card endpoints need a credential with the <strong>Cards</strong> scope and only ever see your business's cards.</p>

      <div class="endpoint" id="ep-token">
        <div class="endpoint-head"><span class="method method-post">POST</span><code>/auth/token</code><span>Get an access token</span></div>
        <p>Exchanges a credential for a token that lasts {{tokenMinutes}} minutes. No <code>Authorization</code> header. Must come from an IP on the credential's whitelist.</p>
        <h4>Body</h4>
        <table class="docs-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Required</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><code>client_id</code></td><td>string</td><td>Yes</td><td>Starts with <code>sa_</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>client_secret</code></td><td>string</td><td>Yes</td><td>Starts with <code>sas_</code></td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <h4>Response <span class="status-code">200</span></h4>
        <table class="docs-table">
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><code>access_token</code></td><td>string</td><td>Send as <code>Authorization: Bearer …</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>token_type</code></td><td>string</td><td>Always <code>Bearer</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>expires_in</code></td><td>number</td><td>Seconds until it expires (3600)</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>scopes</code></td><td>string[]</td><td>What the credential can do, e.g. <code>["Card"]</code></td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <h4>Errors</h4>
        <ul class="docs-errors">
          <li><code>400</code> <code>client_id</code> or <code>client_secret</code> missing</li>
          <li><code>401</code> Invalid client credentials, or the credential is switched off</li>
          <li><code>403</code> IP not on the whitelist, business not approved, no whitelist in production, or five wrong secrets in 15 minutes</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="endpoint" id="ep-list">
        <div class="endpoint-head"><span class="method method-get">GET</span><code>/cards</code><span>List cards</span></div>
        <p>Your cards, newest first.</p>
        <h4>Query parameters</h4>
        <table class="docs-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><code>page</code></td><td>integer</td><td>Default 1</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>pageSize</code></td><td>integer</td><td>Default 10, max 50</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>status</code></td><td>string</td><td><code>Active</code>, <code>Blocked</code>, <code>Terminated</code> or <code>Replaced</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>mobile</code></td><td>string</td><td>Only the cards of this cardholder</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
<pre class="docs-code">curl "{{apiBase}}/cards?status=Active&amp;pageSize=20" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN"</pre>
        <h4>Response <span class="status-code">200</span></h4>
<pre class="docs-code">{
  "page": 1,
  "pageSize": 20,
  "count": 12,
  "data": [ { "reference": "41000002", "name": "Achieng Otieno", "status": "Active", … } ]
}</pre>
        <p class="docs-small">Each item is a <a class="link" href="#card-object">card object</a>.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="endpoint" id="ep-create">
        <div class="endpoint-head"><span class="method method-post">POST</span><code>/cards</code><span>Issue a card</span></div>
        <p>Registers the mobile number as a cardholder with UnionPay the first time it's used, then issues a new card to them. A cardholder can hold several cards.</p>
        <h4>Body</h4>
        <table class="docs-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Required</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><code>mobile</code></td><td>string</td><td>Yes</td><td>Cardholder's Kenyan mobile number</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>name</code></td><td>string</td><td>Yes</td><td>Name on the card, up to 80 characters</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>description</code></td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>Your note, up to 300 characters</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
<pre class="docs-code">curl -X POST {{apiBase}}/cards \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"mobile": "0712345678", "name": "Jane Wanjiku", "description": "Payout card"}'</pre>
        <h4>Response <span class="status-code">201</span></h4>
        <p class="docs-small">The new <a class="link" href="#card-object">card object</a>.</p>
        <h4>Errors</h4>
        <ul class="docs-errors">
          <li><code>400</code> Invalid mobile or name, or UnionPay refused to register the cardholder or create the card (its message is passed on)</li>
          <li><code>502</code> UnionPay could not be reached; nothing was created, so you can retry</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="endpoint" id="ep-get">
        <div class="endpoint-head"><span class="method method-get">GET</span><code>/card/:reference</code><span>Get a card</span></div>
        <p>The card as SaveApp stores it (no call to UnionPay, so it's fast).</p>
        <h4>Path parameters</h4>
        <table class="docs-table"><tbody><tr><td><code>reference</code></td><td>string</td><td>The card's reference</td></tr></tbody></table>
        <h4>Response <span class="status-code">200</span></h4>
        <p class="docs-small">A <a class="link" href="#card-object">card object</a>. <code>404</code> when the card isn't yours or doesn't exist.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="endpoint" id="ep-details">
        <div class="endpoint-head"><span class="method method-get">GET</span><code>/card/:reference/details</code><span>Live details</span></div>
        <p>Asks UnionPay for the card's current status and expiry. SaveApp also updates its stored status if UnionPay reports a change.</p>
        <h4>Response <span class="status-code">200</span></h4>
<pre class="docs-code">{
  "reference": "41000002",
  "maskedNumber": "623401••••••4321",
  "expiry": "12/29",
  "status": "Active"
}</pre>
      </div>

      <div class="endpoint" id="ep-full">
        <div class="endpoint-head"><span class="method method-post">POST</span><code>/card/:reference/details</code><span>Full details, step 1: send the code</span></div>
        <p>Starts the second check for the card's full number, expiry and CVV. SaveApp sends a 6-digit code to your active webhook endpoints as a <a class="link" href="#webhooks"><code>card.details_otp</code></a> event and answers with a <code>challengeId</code>. The code is valid for 5 minutes, and asking again replaces the previous code. You need at least one active webhook endpoint.</p>
<pre class="docs-code">curl -X POST {{apiBase}}/card/41000002/details \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN"</pre>
        <h4>Response <span class="status-code">202</span></h4>
<pre class="docs-code">{
  "challengeId": "chl_9f3c0b6e2d1a4c7b8e5f60a1b2c3d4e5",
  "expiresAt": "2026-11-06T09:05:00.000Z",
  "expiresIn": 300,
  "sentTo": 1
}</pre>
        <h4>Errors</h4>
        <ul class="docs-errors">
          <li><code>400</code> The card is terminated or replaced</li>
          <li><code>409</code> No active webhook endpoint to send the code to</li>
          <li><code>429</code> More than 20 requests in 15 minutes for this credential</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="endpoint" id="ep-full-verify">
        <div class="endpoint-head"><span class="method method-post">POST</span><code>/card/:reference/details/verify</code><span>Full details, step 2: get them</span></div>
        <p>Send back the <code>challengeId</code> and the code from the webhook. The answer has the full card details straight from UnionPay. SaveApp doesn't store them, and the response is marked <code>Cache-Control: no-store</code>; show them to your customer and don't keep them.</p>
        <h4>Body</h4>
        <table class="docs-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Required</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><code>challengeId</code></td><td>string</td><td>Yes</td><td>From step 1</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>otp</code></td><td>string</td><td>Yes</td><td>The 6-digit code from the <code>card.details_otp</code> webhook</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
<pre class="docs-code">curl -X POST {{apiBase}}/card/41000002/details/verify \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"challengeId": "chl_9f3c0b6e2d1a4c7b8e5f60a1b2c3d4e5", "otp": "482913"}'</pre>
        <h4>Response <span class="status-code">200</span></h4>
<pre class="docs-code">{
  "reference": "41000002",
  "name": "Achieng Otieno",
  "cardNumber": "6234010123454321",
  "expiry": "12/29",
  "cvv": "123",
  "status": "Active"
}</pre>
        <h4>Errors</h4>
        <ul class="docs-errors">
          <li><code>400</code> Wrong code (5 tries, then request a new one), expired, already used or replaced, or unknown challenge</li>
          <li><code>502</code> UnionPay could not be reached; request a new code and try again</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="docs-note docs-note-warn">{{icon "triangle-alert" size=16}}<p>Full card details are sensitive. Only request them when your customer asks, never log them, and don't keep them after showing them.</p></div>
      </div>

      <div class="endpoint" id="ep-balance">
        <div class="endpoint-head"><span class="method method-get">GET</span><code>/card/:reference/balance</code><span>Live balance</span></div>
        <h4>Response <span class="status-code">200</span></h4>
<pre class="docs-code">{ "reference": "41000002", "balance": 1250.5, "currency": "KES" }</pre>
      </div>

      <div class="endpoint" id="ep-transactions">
        <div class="endpoint-head"><span class="method method-get">GET</span><code>/card/:reference/transactions</code><span>Live transactions</span></div>
        <h4>Query parameters</h4>
        <table class="docs-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><code>fromDate</code></td><td>string</td><td><code>YYYY-MM-DD</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>toDate</code></td><td>string</td><td><code>YYYY-MM-DD</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>count</code></td><td>integer</td><td>1 to 100</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>page</code></td><td>integer</td><td>From 1</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <h4>Response <span class="status-code">200</span></h4>
<pre class="docs-code">{
  "reference": "41000002",
  "transactions": [ { … as UnionPay reports them … } ],
  "count": 8
}</pre>
        <p class="docs-small">Transactions are passed through as UnionPay reports them. For a reliable record, store the <code>card.transaction</code> webhooks you receive.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="endpoint" id="ep-status">
        <div class="endpoint-head"><span class="method method-post">POST</span><code>/card/:reference/status</code><span>Block, unblock or terminate</span></div>
        <h4>Body</h4>
        <table class="docs-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Required</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><code>action</code></td><td>string</td><td>Yes</td><td><code>block</code> (temporary), <code>unblock</code> or <code>terminate</code> (permanent)</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>reason</code></td><td>string</td><td>Yes</td><td>Up to 200 characters; kept in the card's activity</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
<pre class="docs-code">curl -X POST {{apiBase}}/card/41000002/status \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"action": "block", "reason": "Customer reported the phone stolen"}'</pre>
        <h4>Response <span class="status-code">200</span></h4>
        <p class="docs-small">The updated <a class="link" href="#card-object">card object</a>.</p>
        <h4>Errors</h4>
        <ul class="docs-errors"><li><code>400</code> The card is already terminated or replaced, or UnionPay refused the change</li></ul>
      </div>

      <div class="endpoint" id="ep-replace">
        <div class="endpoint-head"><span class="method method-post">POST</span><code>/card/:reference/replace</code><span>Replace a card</span></div>
        <p>Issues a new card to the same cardholder. The old card becomes <code>Replaced</code> and stops working.</p>
        <h4>Body</h4>
        <table class="docs-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Required</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody><tr><td><code>reason</code></td><td>string</td><td>Yes</td><td>Up to 200 characters</td></tr></tbody>
        </table>
        <h4>Response <span class="status-code">201</span></h4>
        <p class="docs-small">The <strong>new</strong> <a class="link" href="#card-object">card object</a>, with a new reference. Update your records.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="card-object" class="docs-section">
      <h2>The card object</h2>
      <table class="docs-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>reference</code></td><td>string</td><td>The card's id for every card call</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>name</code></td><td>string</td><td>Name on the card</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>description</code></td><td>string</td><td>Your note (may be empty)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>maskedNumber</code></td><td>string</td><td>First six and last four digits. The full number and CVV are only returned by the <a class="link" href="#ep-full">full details</a> check</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>type</code></td><td>string</td><td><code>UnionPay</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>currency</code></td><td>string</td><td><code>KES</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>status</code></td><td>string</td><td><code>Active</code>, <code>Blocked</code>, <code>Terminated</code> or <code>Replaced</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>expiryDate</code></td><td>string or null</td><td>End of the expiry month, when known</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>issuedAt</code></td><td>string</td><td>When the card was issued</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>cardholder.alias</code></td><td>string</td><td>UnionPay's cardholder reference</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>cardholder.mobile</code></td><td>string</td><td>Cardholder mobile, <code>2547XXXXXXXX</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>createdAt</code></td><td>string</td><td>When SaveApp stored the card</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
<pre class="docs-code">{
  "reference": "41000002",
  "name": "Achieng Otieno",
  "description": "Weekly savings payout",
  "maskedNumber": "623401••••••4321",
  "type": "UnionPay",
  "currency": "KES",
  "status": "Active",
  "expiryDate": "2029-12-31T00:00:00.000Z",
  "issuedAt": "2026-10-20T09:12:44.000Z",
  "cardholder": { "alias": "41000001", "mobile": "254700000110" },
  "createdAt": "2026-10-20T09:12:44.000Z"
}</pre>
    </section>

    <section id="webhooks" class="docs-section">
      <h2>Webhooks</h2>
      <p>Add an endpoint under <strong>Integrations › Webhooks</strong>. SaveApp posts a JSON event to it whenever UnionPay reports something about one of your cards. Reply with any <code>2xx</code> status within a few seconds; do the heavy work after replying.</p>
      <table class="docs-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Event</th><th>When</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>card.transaction</code></td><td>A card was used: amount, currency, merchant and whether it was approved.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>card.otp</code></td><td>Your customer is paying with the card and UnionPay needs a one-time code to authorise it. Pass the code to your customer straight away (SMS or in your app); the payment waits for it.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>card.details_otp</code></td><td>You asked for a card's full details. Send the code back to <code>/card/:reference/details/verify</code>.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>webhook.test</code></td><td>You pressed Send test event in the portal.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>Every event has the same envelope:</p>
